#hasheq((campaign . "v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation") (kind . "wave-review") (notes . ("shared git objects: the helper does not rely on alternates or shared-object directories; each private instance is an independent clone of the lazily created per-process baseline so no instance can read or write another instance's object store, and real clone semantics (packing, ref rewriting, HEAD selection) are exercised rather than a pure file copy of .git" "ref leakage: private clones own their refs, packed-refs, and index; the contract suite proves a commit made in one concurrent instance leaves the sibling's refs, the sibling's working tree, and the immutable baseline byte-identical, and origin/main is repointed inside each instance's own remote config (offline stand-in) instead of sharing a remote ref" "global env and CWD: instances are created under fresh private temp roots, tests switch CWD into their own instance and mutate environment variables, and the stress suite proves env/CWD mutation in one instance cannot be observed from a concurrently created instance; no fixed /tmp path is used — all roots come from the system temp directory with unique randomized names and canonicalization checks" "event-bus reuse: the session template path allocates a fresh session id, event bus, and registries per copied instance; the contract suite appends to one instance's session log and asserts the sibling log and the immutable template source remain unchanged" "cleanup masking: instances can be destroyed in arbitrary concurrent orders and destruction is idempotent — destroying twice, or destroying while a sibling still lives, neither raises nor removes the sibling or the template source, so cleanup can never mask a failing assertion by throwing late" "loss of real git behavior: git-unavailable is an explicit skip through the helper's guarded check, never a silent pass; hermetic per-instance user identity is preserved; family-specific branch, commit, dirty-tree, delivery, and orphan assertions were kept in their owner files, and no product session/Git/worktree implementation changed" "scope disclosure: the previous attempt failed delivery verification with no wave-evidence/review/validation records delivered and an order-dependent origin/main ambiguity in the delivery-verifier sandbox; this attempt pins the sandbox to the two-tier checkout layout (base dir with git root at q/ inside it), delivers all three records, and re-verifies every focused gate green before returning")) (reviewer . "q-agent-independent-review") (scope . "tests/helpers/private-fixture-templates.rkt; tests/fixtures/session-template/; tests/test-private-fixture-templates.rkt; measured-family migrations in test-golden-flows.rkt, test-gsd-delivery-verifier.rkt, test-gsd-wave-worktree.rkt, test-gsd-branch-delivery-verification.rkt (shared sandbox builder only); ledger and ownership map W6 rows; w6-fixtures-after manifest") (status . "completed") (verdict . "pass") (wave . "W6"))
